    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 4th slate with a clear focus on stolen base efficiency and exploitable pitching matchups. Our strongest play of the day is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who sits in a tier of his own against Leahy. His elite speed profile remains our primary engine, and a favorable park factor combined with a significant +13% SP Skill advantage cements his status as a \"must-start.\" Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) offers substantial value against Kelly; despite a minor negative BvP flag, the +19% SP Skill boost and the +13% dynamic platoon edge against the righty keep him firmly in the elite start category. While **Yordan Alvarez** (58.67) presents a lower efficiency score than typical, his 0.477 xwOBA remains the most potent tool in our lineup, and he remains locked into the OF2 slot despite the tough assignment against the right-handed Rasmussen.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luke Raley** (58.60), who fell just shy of the threshold for a start. While he benefits from a strong SP Skill matchup against Bieber, his lower base projection relative to the depth of our outfield depth\u2014specifically **Casey Schmitt** (60.44), whose massive +14% park advantage and +19% SP skill boost pushed him over the top\u2014necessitated keeping him in reserve. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.90); facing the elite arm of Gilbert is a significant hurdle that drags his efficiency down near our floor. We will be monitoring the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, **Zac Veen**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** throughout the day to ensure our depth remains ready should any late lineup changes or weather-related disruptions force a reshuffle of the current rotation.",
